'''Pochi''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that could be obtained from the [[Nebaaru-kun and Nyanpazuru Collaboration Event|Nebaaru-kun and Nyanpazuru Collaboration]] [[Cat Capsule#Collaboration Event Capsule|Event Cat Capsule]]. It was added in [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 263
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Pochi
|name2 = Tank Pochi
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Tank Pochi '''at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
The only thing worth knowing about Pochi is how poor of an attempt he is to make a [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critter]]. Pochi lacks everything that a critter needs. He is spammable, sure, but his chance is nonexistent, his speed isn't fast enough, and his range is too low. This means that his otherwise good spammability doesn't allow him to be a useful critical hitter. Putting [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] doesn't help this aspect either, as spammability is the only thing he has, and it's nullified by everything bad about him. If you want a critter, you should just invest in [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]], especially with [[Talents]]. Other good units would be [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]], [[Marauder Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Paladin Cat]] and [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]]. At the very least, he can help with [[User Rank]], but that's the lowest you can go.

You are best using him as an attacker very early on. His attack power is decent, and his attack rate is great. He can help you with the [[Empire of Cats]] stages quite a bit, at least until you face off against [[Teacher Bun Bun]]. After that, he's immediately useless.

